<%# The lab layout.

    It publishes the SAME data attribute a host publishes — data-solana-network,
    carrying Solana::Network.describe — because that is the contract the shipped
    guard reads. A hand-set attribute with different keys would let the specs pass
    over a guard that could never read a real host's page.

    Alpine and the guard both arrive by <script src>, pointing at the real files
    e2e/boot.rb copied into public/e2e. Alpine is DEFERRED so the modal host's
    store registration (which runs inline, in the host partial) lands first —
    the host's own comment explains why that order is load-bearing. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>solana-studio e2e lab</title>
    <script src="/e2e/js/solana_studio/network_guard.js"></script>
    <%# The redirect-transport set, loaded the way a host loads it: plain
        <script src> off the REAL files e2e/boot.rb copied out of app/assets.
        Order matters — redirect_provider and wallet_ops both read
        window.SolanaStudio.walletTransport at call time, and wallet_ops reaches
        for walletJournal, so the core comes first. They define no globals of
        their own beyond SolanaStudio.* and are inert until a page calls them,
        which is why every lab page can carry them without affecting the others. %>
    <script src="/e2e/js/solana_studio/wallet_transport.js"></script>
    <script src="/e2e/js/solana_studio/redirect_provider.js"></script>
    <script src="/e2e/js/solana_studio/wallet_journal.js"></script>
    <script src="/e2e/js/solana_studio/wallet_ops.js"></script>
  </head>
  <%# `x-data` ON THE BODY is a HOST responsibility, not decoration.
      studio-engine's modal host roots itself at a bare
      <template x-if="$store.modals.current()"> with no x-data of its own, and
      Alpine v3 only walks trees beneath an x-data root — so without this the
      host's template is never processed, the modal never opens, and the page
      looks perfectly fine in curl. turf-monster's layout carries the same bare
      `x-data` on <body> for the same reason. The lab is the host here, so the
      lab supplies it. %>
  <body x-data class="bg-page text-body" data-solana-network="<%= @network_json %>" data-solana-cluster="<%= lab_cluster %>">
    <%= yield %>
    <script defer src="/e2e/js/studio/alpine.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
